From: Grische <opensource@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:07:01 +0200
Subject: wifi: ath10k: reset the HTT tx queue state when the firmware starts

The host allocates struct htt_q_state at the first start of the device
and keeps it, together with the push-pull mode fields, until the driver
is removed. ath10k_htt_tx_start() returns early on every later start,
so a firmware booted by ath10k_core_restart() or by a later
ath10k_start() inherits the queue state and the mode of the previous
firmware.

If the old firmware was in push-pull mode, the host stays in push-pull
after the restart. It pushes nothing and waits for fetch indications,
while a firmware with WMI_SERVICE_TX_MODE_DYNAMIC starts in push mode
and fetches nothing. No data frame leaves the radio until the new
firmware reports its mode. On a QCA9984 this took 2.2 s after the
restart had completed, and every frame queued in that time, unicast
and multicast alike, waited for it or was lost. The count and map
entries of the old peers stay set as well, although the new firmware
assigns its peer ids from scratch.

Return the mode fields and the queue state buffer to their state at the
first start before the firmware is booted, and sync the buffer to the
device.

Tested-on: QCA9984 hw1.0 PCI 10.4-3.9.0.2-00157

Fixes: 426e10eaf76d ("ath10k: implement push-pull tx")
Assisted-by: LLM sparse
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_tx.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_tx.c
@@ -440,6 +440,26 @@ static int ath10k_htt_tx_alloc_txq(struc
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void ath10k_htt_tx_txq_reset(struct ath10k_htt *htt)
+{
+	struct ath10k *ar = htt->ar;
+	size_t size = sizeof(*htt->tx_q_state.vaddr);
+
+	spin_lock_bh(&htt->tx_lock);
+
+	htt->tx_q_state.enabled = false;
+	htt->tx_q_state.mode = HTT_TX_MODE_SWITCH_PUSH;
+	htt->tx_q_state.num_push_allowed = 0;
+
+	if (htt->tx_q_state.vaddr) {
+		memset(htt->tx_q_state.vaddr, 0, size);
+		dma_sync_single_for_device(ar->dev, htt->tx_q_state.paddr,
+					   size, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+	}
+
+	spin_unlock_bh(&htt->tx_lock);
+}
+
 static void ath10k_htt_tx_free_txdone_fifo(struct ath10k_htt *htt)
 {
 	WARN_ON(!kfifo_is_empty(&htt->txdone_fifo));
@@ -510,8 +530,14 @@ int ath10k_htt_tx_start(struct ath10k_ht
 	spin_lock_init(&htt->tx_lock);
 	idr_init(&htt->pending_tx);
 
-	if (htt->tx_mem_allocated)
+	if (htt->tx_mem_allocated) {
+		/* The queue state buffer and the push-pull mode outlive the
+		 * firmware. Return them to their state at the first start,
+		 * so a new firmware does not inherit those of the old one.
+		 */
+		ath10k_htt_tx_txq_reset(htt);
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	if (ar->bus_param.dev_type == ATH10K_DEV_TYPE_HL)
 		return 0;
